  "name": "FACTOR-VIII (STAT)",
  "code": "1548",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>Factor VIII is a <strong data-start=\"93\" data-end=\"113\">clotting protein</strong> (anti-hemophilic factor) essential for proper blood coagulation. Deficiency or dysfunction of this factor leads to <strong data-start=\"229\" data-end=\"245\">Hemophilia A</strong>, a genetic bleeding disorder.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Factor VIII Activity</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>&gt;150%</strong></td>\n<td>Elevated &mdash; could be due to inflammation, pregnancy, liver disease, or as a risk factor for thrombosis</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>50&ndash;150%</strong></td>\n<td>Normal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>30&ndash;50%</strong></td>\n<td>Mild deficiency &mdash; may cause bleeding with trauma or surgery</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>5&ndash;30%</strong></td>\n<td>Moderate deficiency &mdash; spontaneous bleeding possible</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>&lt;5%</strong></td>\n<td>Severe deficiency &mdash; frequent spontaneous bleeding episodes</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"1115\" data-end=\"1145\"><strong data-start=\"1119\" data-end=\"1145\">Clinical Significance:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1147\" data-end=\"1520\">\n<li data-start=\"1147\" data-end=\"1363\">\n<p data-start=\"1149\" data-end=\"1164\"><strong data-start=\"1149\" data-end=\"1164\">Low Levels:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1167\" data-end=\"1363\">\n<li data-start=\"1167\" data-end=\"1209\">\n<p data-start=\"1169\" data-end=\"1209\"><strong data-start=\"1169\" data-end=\"1185\">Hemophilia A</strong> (inherited or acquired)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1212\" data-end=\"1231\">\n<p data-start=\"1214\" data-end=\"1231\"><strong data-start=\"1214\" data-end=\"1231\">Liver disease</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1234\" data-end=\"1284\">\n<p data-start=\"1236\" data-end=\"1284\"><strong data-start=\"1236\" data-end=\"1284\">Disseminated Intravascular Coagulation (DIC)</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1287\" data-end=\"1313\">\n<p data-start=\"1289\" data-end=\"1313\"><strong data-start=\"1289\" data-end=\"1313\">Vitamin K deficiency</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1316\" data-end=\"1363\">\n<p data-start=\"1318\" data-end=\"1363\"><strong data-start=\"1318\" data-end=\"1363\">Autoimmune inhibitors against Factor VIII</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1365\" data-end=\"1520\">\n<p data-start=\"1367\" data-end=\"1383\"><strong data-start=\"1367\" data-end=\"1383\">High Levels:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1386\" data-end=\"1520\">\n<li data-start=\"1386\" data-end=\"1410\">\n<p data-start=\"1388\" data-end=\"1410\"><strong data-start=\"1388\" data-end=\"1410\">Acute inflammation</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1413\" data-end=\"1428\">\n<p data-start=\"1415\" data-end=\"1428\"><strong data-start=\"1415\" data-end=\"1428\">Pregnancy</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1431\" data-end=\"1459\">\n<p data-start=\"1433\" data-end=\"1459\"><strong data-start=\"1433\" data-end=\"1459\">Oral contraceptive use</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1462\" data-end=\"1520\">\n<p data-start=\"1464\" data-end=\"1520\"><strong data-start=\"1464\" data-end=\"1520\">Thrombotic risk (e.g., deep vein thrombosis, stroke)</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>",
